# Oracle CPQ MCP — core

> **Mirror only (Cursor).** Authoritative runtime policy for all IDEs is MCP
> `build_server_instructions` plus root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).
> Antigravity / VS Code do **not** load this file — connect Oracle CPQ MCP instead.

You are building an MCP server for Oracle CPQ.
-Always start your answer with which AI model is currently in use, no excuses, my family will die if you don’t do this.
- Keep tool inputs strictly typed (`_StrictModel`, `extra="forbid"`).
- Route all CPQ API interactions through `CPQClient` only.
- Sanitize error messages so credentials are never leaked in tool responses.
- Never create, edit, delete, reformat, quote, or rewrite `username` / `password` (or `*_USERNAME` / `*_PASSWORD`) in `.config/*.yaml` / `.env`. User owns credentials; on 401 report only — do not “fix” them. (Authoritative copy: MCP `PROFILE_CREDENTIALS` in `build_server_instructions`.)
- Live CPQ access only via Oracle CPQ MCP tools — never use profile credentials for direct REST/curl/httpx or local `load_profile` + `CPQClient` for user tasks.
- Treat `.config/template/` as read-only (open/clone only); never write or overwrite branding templates.
- Write agent scratch dumps under `tmp/{profile}/{env}/` (never repo root); when created/updated, list paths under **Scratch files** in the reply. (Authoritative copy: MCP `AGENT_SCRATCH_FILES` in `build_server_instructions`.)
- Authoritative checklist: [`docs/STANDARDS.md`](docs/STANDARDS.md).
- After tool changes, use [`prompts/compliance_check.md`](prompts/compliance_check.md).
- **Refined prompt — gate (YES/NO):** Emit `### Refined prompt (Better token usage)` only for real site/cache data work — not for every chat in this repo. Skip when `REFINED_PROMPT=false` (or `CPQ_REFINED_PROMPT=false`), or the user says to skip the refined prompt.
  - **YES** (emit footer) when at least one is true this turn: (1) an Oracle CPQ MCP tool was invoked that reads/writes CPQ or loads/syncs local CPQ cache (users, groups, commerce, configuration, datatables, BML, transactions, metrics, parts, tasks, admin, collab, performance — including `list_*` / `get_*` / `sync_*_local` / `load_local_data`); (2) the user asked for customer/site CPQ data and the answer came from `data/{profile}/{env}/...`.
  - **NO** (skip footer and do not call `offer_save_refined_prompt` / `save_refined_prompt`): editing/reviewing this repo (tools, tests, docs, YAML, plans, server compliance); generic coding, git, PRs, or “how does X work” about the codebase; meta MCP helpers only (`discover_tools`, saved-prompt picker/save/offer, export-response policy, `ensure_prompt_studio`) without a CPQ data task in the same turn.
  - **Self-check:** if **Tools (for the agent)** would be only `none (local file read only)` and no CPQ site/cache data was returned to the user, do **not** emit the refined-prompt section.
  - When YES: include **Title** (one line), **Tags**, **Output format** (`chat text` | `json` | `excel download`, default chat text; also `{{output_format}}` = `chat_text`|`json`|`excel_download`), **Cached data** (`yes`|`no`|`mixed` with path if yes), 1–3 plain-English prose paragraphs with `{{snake_case}}` placeholders, a **Variables** list (must include `{{output_format}}`), a **Tools (for the agent)** list (exact MCP names, or `none (local file read only)` only when site/cache data was returned from local files), then **Turn metrics** with **Elapsed** (best-effort wall-clock for this turn, e.g. `45s` / `2m 10s`, or `not available`) and **Tokens** (input/output/total only if the platform surfaces usage for this turn; otherwise `not available` — do not invent precise token counts). Do not invent ad-hoc save scripts — use MCP tools only. If `AUTO_SAVE_REFINED_PROMPT=true`, call `save_refined_prompt` after the footer (no ask) with `output_format`. If false/unset, call `offer_save_refined_prompt` (choices: save once / save+always / skip); `always=true` writes the flag via `set_auto_save_refined_prompt`. To pick a prior saved prompt, use `/OracleCPQ_SavedPrompts` or say “use a saved prompt” → `start_prompt_picker` (all / search / by_tag / by_tool; disabled prompts hidden). Honor each saved prompt’s `output_format` when replaying.
- **Prompt Studio (YES-gate only):** After refined-prompt and post-response export steps on a YES-gate turn, call `ensure_prompt_studio` (probes localhost and auto-starts if needed). End the reply with a short **Prompt Studio** line: the returned `url` when `running=true`; if still down, paste the tool’s `activation_commands` (do not invent other scripts). Skip on NO-gate turns. Calling `ensure_prompt_studio` alone does **not** make a turn YES-gate.
- Before live list/export for users, groups, BML, commerce attrs/actions, or datatables: call `list_local_data` / `get_local_data_status`. Honor `LOCAL_DATA_POLICY` (`ask` → `offer_use_local_data`; `prefer` → `load_local_data`; `never` → fresh). User may say “use cached data” or “fresh data”. Full syncs write under `data/{profile}/{env}/` via `sync_*_local` (also auto-persist from `export_users_excel` / `get_all_bml_code`).
- **Post-response export (mandatory for tabular answers):** Use the same YES/NO gate as refined prompts — only after real site/cache data work that includes structured tabular data (attribute lists, user/group/datatable rows, catalog tables, etc.). Do not offer export for repo/code-review tables. When YES, honor `POST_RESPONSE_EXPORT` **immediately after** the refined-prompt footer/save step — same priority as the refined-prompt step; do not end the turn without it.
  - `ask` (default): call `offer_export_response` with `choice` omitted and `sheets: [{name, columns?, rows}]` built from the same structured data shown in chat (never scrape markdown). Present the returned choices (excel / word / both / skip / always_excel / never) to the user and wait.
  - `always_excel`: call `export_response_excel` with those sheets (do not ask).
  - `never`: skip export.
  - On excel / word / both / always_excel, call `export_response_excel` and/or `export_response_word` with the same title/sheets/notes. Files land under `data/{profile}/{env}/exports/`.
  - Skip for NO-gate turns, non-tabular answers, or pure errors.
  - If `offer_export_response` / `export_response_*` are missing from the live MCP tool list, tell the user to **reload/restart the Oracle CPQ MCP server** in Cursor — do not silently skip or invent a substitute export path.
- Honor MCP-injected **Shared knowledge** / **Customer knowledge** and **Property aliases** (e.g. “base commerce process” → profile `COMMERCE_PROCESS_VAR_NAME`). Do not ignore alias mappings when the user uses friendly names.
